[I] A Git-compatible VCS that is both simple and powerful

[T] Jujutsu (jj) is a powerful version control system for software projects.
[T] You use it to get a copy of your code, track changes to the code, and
[T] finally publish those changes for others to see and use.

[U] https://jj-vcs.github.io/jj/

[A] Google LLC
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/development
[F] CROSS

[L] APL
[V] 0.45.1

[D] fcf8a0bc64ce499894d12d5156f47254f87b5f06b9b9541aba39b2ae jj-0.45.1.tar.gz https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj/archive/v0.45.1/

rungpepinstall=0 cargoinstopt=
atstage cross && hook_add postmake 5 "install target/${arch_target}/*/jj $root$bindir/"
atstage native && hook_add postmake 5 "install target/*/jj $root$bindir/"
